# Normalize line endings so a Windows checkout and a Linux checkout produce the
# same bytes. Typst and Node read either, but a mixed tree makes diffs noisy.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Vendored third-party sources keep their upstream bytes exactly: rewriting line
# endings inside a redistributed package would make it disagree with the copy it
# is meant to be, and would obscure whether anything else was changed.
packages/dsh-presentation/vendor/ -text

# Binary assets are never line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.exe binary
